sentences.t:
Ut vidit socios: “Tempus desistere pugnae;
solus ego in Pallanta feror, soli mihi Pallas
debetur; cuperem ipse parens spectator adesset.”

sentences.l:
When he saw his comrades: “Time to cease from the fight;
alone I against Pallas am borne, to me alone Pallas
is owed; I could wish his father himself were here to watch.”

“Stands for each his own day, short and beyond repair the time
for all is of life: but fame to extend by deeds,
this is of valour the work.

sentences.t:
Quem Turnus super adsistens,
“Arcades, haec, inquit, memores mea dicta referte
Euandro;

sentences.l:
Over whom Turnus standing,
“Arcadians, these, he says, mindful my words carry back
to Evander;
